@startuml GameFlow
!theme mars

state GameTurn as "Game Turn" {
  state AETurn as "Anglo-Egyptian Player Turn" {
    state AEMove as "1. Movement Phase"
    state AEFire as "2. Fire Combat Phase" {
      state DervDefFire as "a. Dervish Defensive Fire"
      state AEOffFire as "b. Anglo-Egyptian Offensive Fire" {
        state DirectFire as "1. Direct Fire Subphase"
        state MaximHow as "2. Maxim Second Fire &\nHowitzer Subphase"
      }
    }
    state AEMelee as "3. Melee Phase"
  }

  state DervTurn as "Dervish Player Turn" {
    state DervMove as "1. Movement Phase"
    state DervFire as "2. Fire Combat Phase" {
      state AEDefFire as "a. Anglo-Egyptian Defensive Fire" {
        state AEDirect as "1. Direct Fire Subphase"
        state AEMaxim as "2. Maxim Second Fire &\nHowitzer Subphase"
      }
      state DervOffFire as "b. Dervish Offensive Fire\n(Direct only)"
    }
    state DervMelee as "3. Melee Phase"
  }

  state AdvanceTurn as "Advance Game Turn marker"
}

state SetupPhase as "Setup Phase"
[*] --> SetupPhase
SetupPhase --> GameTurn : Both ready

state first_move <<choice>>
GameTurn --> first_move
first_move --> AETurn : Campaign
first_move --> DervTurn : Historical / FoK

note right of first_move
  FoK special rules (§9.343-§9.345):
  • Both use Dervish RET
  • Dervish controls North Fort
  • Gunboat White/Blue Nile crossing
end note

' === When A-E goes first (Campaign) ===
AETurn --> AEMove
AEMove --> DervDefFire : Done moving
DervDefFire --> DirectFire : Dervish done firing
DirectFire --> MaximHow : A-E done allocating\n& resolving direct fire
MaximHow --> AEMelee : A-E done with\nMaxim/Howitzer fire
AEMelee --> DervTurn : [Campaign]\nfollowing A-E turn

' === When Dervish goes first (Historical, FoK) ===
DervTurn --> DervMove
DervMove --> AEDirect : Done moving
AEDirect --> AEMaxim : A-E done with\ndefensive direct fire
AEMaxim --> DervOffFire : A-E done with\ndefensive Maxim/How
DervOffFire --> DervMelee : Dervish done with\noffensive fire
DervMelee --> AETurn : [Historical, FoK]\nfollowing Dervish turn

' === Both paths converge ===
AEMelee --> AdvanceTurn : [Historical, FoK]\nA-E 2nd turn done
DervMelee --> AdvanceTurn : [Campaign]\nDervish 2nd turn done

AdvanceTurn --> GameTurn : Next hour
GameTurn --> [*] : Scenario end\ncondition met

' === Setup Phase ===
note right of SetupPhase
  Setup (§9.11, §9.21, §9.32):
  • Place units per scenario instructions
  • Both players ready → first Player Turn
end note

' === Movement Phase Details ===
note right of AEMove
  A-E Movement (§5):
  • Move units up to MA (§5.11, §5.12)
  • Zariba construction (A-E only) (§5.3)
  • Transport Friendlies (A-E only) (§5.21)
  • Friendlies Brigade (§6.52)
  • Dervish desertion roll
    (campaign, first night, once) (§8.2)
  • Nile impassable to land (§5.22)
  • Walled city: Khalifa only (§5.23)
  • Gunboat: up/downstream (§5.24)
  • Forts immobile (§5.25)
  • Reinforcements on schedule (§9.112, §9.113)
end note

note right of DervMove
  Dervish Movement (§5):
  • Move units up to MA (§5.11, §5.12)
  • Dervish desertion roll
    (already resolved on first
    night during A-E turn) (§8.2)
  • Nile impassable to land (§5.22)
  • Walled city: Khalifa only (§5.23)
  • Gunboat: up/downstream (§5.24)
  • Forts immobile (§5.25)
  • Reinforcements on schedule (§9.112, §9.113)
end note

' === Fire Combat Resolution (same for all subphases) ===
note right of DervDefFire
  Defensive Fire (§6.7):
  • Voluntary — may choose not to fire (§6.12)
  • Unitary factor — may not divide (§6.13)
  • Stack may split targets (§6.15)
  • Halving rounds down, min 1 (§6.16)
  Resolution per attack (§6.4):
  1. Check Line of Sight (§6.21)
     (howitzers: ignore LOS)
  2. Range Effects Table (§6.22)
     (multiplier: ×3, ×2, ×1, ×½)
  3. Sum fire factors attacking
     target hex (§6.14)
  4. Terrain Effects Chart (§6.23)
     (defender terrain mod)
  5. Roll 1d10 + mods → CRT (§CRT)
  • A-E direct fire: +1 accuracy (§6.24)
  • A-E brigade integrity: +1 (§5.54)
  • A-E leaders no ZOC (§5.41)
  • Leaders zero fire factor (§6.51)
  • No advance after combat
    (defensive fire) (§6.7)
end note

note right of DirectFire
  Direct Fire (§6.41):
  Same resolution as defensive (§6.4),
  then:
  • If target hex vacated:
    adjacent participants may
    advance after combat (§6.82)
    (not artillery, not across
    walls/khors)
end note

note right of MaximHow
  A-E only (§6.42, §6.64):
  • Maxims fire second time
    (or once if skipped direct)
  • Named gunboats fire
    howitzers (LOS-free):
    - Range 4-10 hexes
    - 2 die rolls: CRT + impact
    - Hit on impact 7-10
    - Scatter 1-6 per scattergram
    - Must apply even to friendlies
    - None at night (§8.1)
  • Advance after combat per
    direct fire rules (§6.82)
end note

note right of DervOffFire
  Dervish Offensive Fire (§6.8):
  • Direct Fire only (§6.41)
  • Dervish Range Effects Table (§6.22)
  • No +1 accuracy bonus
  • No Maxim/Howitzer subphase
  • Advance after combat allowed (§6.82)
end note

' === Melee Details ===
note right of AEMelee
  Melee (§7):
  • Adjacent target only (§7.2)
  • Simultaneous resolution (§7.3)
  • Both roll CRT + melee mods (§7.7)
    Dervish: +2   A-E: +1
  • Losses from meleeing units first
  • Cavalry/camel: retreat 2 hexes
    from infantry (once/turn) (§7.5)
  • Dervish MUST advance if hex vacated (§7.6)
  • A-E MAY advance if hex vacated (§7.6)
  • A-E leaders may not melee attack
    (Dervish leaders may) (§7.4, §6.51)
  • Forts: defensive only (-3) (§6.54)
  • RE demolition (A-E only): (§6.53)
    destroy fort or breach wall
end note

note right of DervMelee
  Melee (§7):
  Same as A-E Melee
  Dervish MUST advance (§7.6)
  A-E MAY advance (§7.6)
end note

' === Night Turn ===
note left of AdvanceTurn
  Night turns (§8, §8.1):
  • A-E movement halved
  • No A-E howitzer fire
  • All ranges halved
    (range 1 stays 1)
  • Range effects same as day
end note

@enduml
